  "distractor_rules": {
    "roots": [
      "Four spellings of one word. Exactly one is the real spelling.",
      "The real word has an open syllable that ends in one vowel letter, and that vowel is long.",
      "Distractors are misspellings of that same word, never a different real word.",
      "Tier 1 distractors drop a vowel, scramble letters, or repeat an extra letter.",
      "Tier 2 distractors double the consonant after the open vowel, or replace that vowel with a vowel team.",
      "Tier 3 distractors are one letter off on a two-syllable or three-syllable word, usually a doubled consonant that would close the syllable.",
      "The stem is a short meaning clue. Do not write the correct spelling in the stem.",
      "Use whole words only. No isolated sounds, no IPA, no audio file names, and no brand names.",
      "Stay in a kid world of school, home, food, pets, play, family, and weather.",
      "Every stem word comes from the roots word list or allowed_extra_words, or is the token <NAME>."
    ]
  },
